A vulnerability was found in <a href="https://vuldb.com/product/racktables">RackTables up to 0.22.0/e5fff9f8aab339798ed47e8c6d7d977ed97a82bd</a>. It has been classified as <a href="https://vuldb.com/kb/risk">problematic</a>. This vulnerability affects unknown code. The manipulation leads to cross-site request forgery.

This vulnerability is uniquely identified as <a href="https://vuldb.com/cve/CVE-2026-18819">CVE-2026-18819</a>. The attack is possible to be carried out remotely. Moreover, an exploit is present.

The project maintainer confirms: &quot;[I]t seems plausible, in that RackTables does not at this time have any CSRF prevention. You may assign a CVE ID to this, but there is no guarantee it will be handled in urgent, or even timely, manner, or at all.&quot;
